        },
        {
          "p": 25,
          "text": "Proof. The regular convex polytopes in dimension 5 and above comprise exactly three families: the n-simplex, the n-hypercube, and the n-cross-polytope (Coxeter classification). The cells of the 5-simplex are 5 tetrahedral 4-cells. The cells of the 5-hypercube are 10 tesseract 4-cells. The cells of the 5-cross-polytope are 32 pentachoron 4-cells. None has 120-cell cells. The recursion condition CELL(CARRIER(4)) ≅ CARRIER(3) = 120-cell is unsatisfiable. □"
        },
        {
          "p": 26,
          "text": "The recursion therefore has exactly three levels. CARRIER(1) is 2-dimensional, CARRIER(2) is 3-dimensional, CARRIER(3) is 4-dimensional, and no CARRIER(4) exists within the class of regular convex polytopes."
