        },
        {
          "p": 55,
          "text": "Theorem 3.1 (μ at Depth 3, Carrier Pair). μ(120-cell) > 0."
        },
        {
          "p": 56,
          "text": "Proof. D(120-cell) = 600-cell. Sym = H₄, |H₄| = 14400. D(120-cell) ≇ 120-cell as realized objects: |V(120-cell)| = 600 ≠ |V(600-cell)| = 120, |F₃(120-cell)| = 120 dodecahedral cells ≠ |F₃(600-cell)| = 600 tetrahedral cells. Construct: Cₘ = F₃(120-cell) (120 dodecahedral cells, maintenance carrier). Cₐ = V(600-cell) (120 vertices, action carrier). |Cₘ| = |Cₐ| = 120, both nonempty. H₄ acts transitively on both (flag-transitivity of regular polytopes implies transitivity on each carrier set). Both are single orbits, hence H₄-invariant. Supports are geometrically distinct (cells of one polytope versus vertices of another). All conditions of D0.2 satisfied. □"
