        {
          "p": 67,
          "text": "The non-compositionality is not a deficiency of the definition. It is a structural feature of duality under cellular decomposition. The self-duality of a polytope is a global property that does not reduce to the self-duality of its cells. The 24-cell’s octahedral cells are individually capable of separating maintenance from action, but the 24-cell as a whole cannot, because F₄ symmetry acts transitively on the entire cell set and forces invariant-subset rigidity at the global level."
