        {
          "p": 68,
          "text": "5. Trust Boundary Topology"
        },
        {
          "p": 69,
          "text": "Adjacent dodecahedral cells in the 120-cell share a pentagonal face. The pentagon is a semantic domain in the Fragility Topology (12 pentagonal faces per dodecahedral cell). When two cells share a pentagonal face, they share a semantic domain."
        },
        {
          "p": 70,
          "text": "Theorem 5.1 (Coordination Topology). The cell-adjacency graph of the 120-cell is isomorphic to the vertex-edge skeleton of the 600-cell."
        },
        {
          "p": 71,
          "text": "Proof. The 120-cell has 120 dodecahedral cells. Two cells are adjacent when they share a pentagonal face. The dual of the 120-cell is the 600-cell with 120 vertices. Duality maps cells of P to vertices of D(P) and adjacency of cells to adjacency of vertices. The cell-adjacency graph of the 120-cell is therefore the 1-skeleton of the 600-cell. □"
